 <kendinikertenkelebek@me.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:59:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(archinfo): add a table of supported architectures

PiSi knew one architecture at a time and hard-coded x86 facts in several
places: the default host triplet and flags (i686), the kernel ARCH= mapping
(only i686 -> i386) and the kernel image path (arch/x86/boot/bzImage).
Supporting aarch64 means every such place has to ask one source instead.

pisi/archinfo.py holds that source: for x86_64, i686 and aarch64 it lists
the canonical name, accepted aliases (amd64, arm64, ...), the GNU host
triplet, default compiler flags, the kernel ARCH= value, the kernel image
path and which architecture-bound build types exist (emul32 on x86_64,
pae on i686). canonical(), same() and excluded() compare architecture
names by meaning, so '<ExcludeArch>arm64</ExcludeArch>' excludes aarch64;
an unknown name raises instead of silently never matching. machine()
maps os.uname() to a canonical name.

Nothing uses the table yet; the following commits switch the callers.
---
 pisi/archinfo.py | 159 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 159 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 pisi/archinfo.py

diff --git a/pisi/archinfo.py b/pisi/archinfo.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d8354e5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pisi/archinfo.py
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
+#
